# posteriordb_processed/ IS committed, as of 2026-09-09.
#
# It was ignored as "regenerable via run_validation.sh", which was true on a
# machine with python3, numpy, and a clone of stan-dev/posteriordb -- and false
# everywhere else. On 2026-09-09 a fleet posteriordb run found nothing to do on
# all three remote hosts: the directory was absent, the harness listed zero
# posteriors, and the run reported success by having nothing to fail. None of
# those hosts has the preprocessing toolchain, and putting it on a FreeBSD
# Kepler and a Jetson to regenerate a fixed input is worse than storing 28 MB.
#
# Committing them makes `git pull` sufficient to reproduce a verification run,
# which is the property the fleet needs.
